    and the Rotary menu, is docs/3110-Website-Moderator-Guide.md in the website's repository. -#}
<div class="wrap section narrow prose">
  <h1>Moderator guide</h1>
  <p class="lead">You check what clubs and members send before it appears on the district website, and you keep the district's records up to date. Everything is done on your phone, on the <a href="/desk/">moderation desk</a>. You do not need Google Sheets.</p>
  <p><strong>When the website changes:</strong> what you approve, hide or correct appears at the next website update, at about 9 am, 1 pm, 6 pm or 10 pm. Every correction asks for a short reason and is kept in a change log, so it can be undone.</p>

  <h2 id="start">Getting started</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the desk from the <strong>Open the moderation desk</strong> button in any moderator email. After the first time, your phone remembers it.</li>
    <li>Type your email address (the one the district has on its moderators list) and tap <strong>Send me a code</strong>.</li>
    <li>An email arrives with a 6-digit code and a <strong>Sign in</strong> button. Use either once, within 15 minutes.</li>
    <li>You stay signed in on that phone for 7 days. On someone else's phone, tap <strong>Sign out</strong> when you finish.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>The <strong>हिन्दी</strong> button at the top switches the desk's own words to Hindi. What clubs typed stays as they typed it.</p>

  <h2 id="rules">Three rules for everyone</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your name stays private.</strong> Answer the public and clubs only from the desk, never from your own email or phone. The desk sends from the district account, signed "Rotary District 3110".</li>
    <li><strong>Nothing personal goes on the website.</strong> No personal mobile numbers or emails, no UPI or bank details, no children's names. Tap <strong>Correct</strong> to remove them, or reject.</li>
    <li><strong>When unsure, reject kindly.</strong> Write a reason the sender can act on ("Please send a photo of the work itself"). They can send it again.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="content">Content moderators</h2>
  <p>You check activities, events, club profile updates and public services (blood banks, eye care and so on). Please try to check each item within 48 hours. If you look after one area of the district (the Agra, Bareilly or Kanpur clubs), you get emails for those clubs only, and they come first on the desk; the rest follow under <strong>Other areas</strong>.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>From the email:</strong> each new item sends you an email with its text, photos and two big buttons, <strong>Approve</strong> and <strong>Reject</strong>. They open the desk, where one more tap confirms. That extra tap is on purpose. The buttons work only on a phone where you are signed in to the desk; anywhere else it asks for your code first, so please do not forward these emails.</li>
    <li><strong>On the desk, To check → Clean:</strong> activities in which the checks found nothing. Glance at each line and its photos. Untick anything that looks wrong (a child named, an unsuitable photo, not really a club activity): it moves to Needs a look. Then tap <strong>Approve the ticked</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>To check → Needs a look:</strong> everything else, as a card, with the reason at the top: a possible duplicate, a missing photo, a future date, payment details, photos without the consent tick, a District mark (check the district organised it) or a campaign count (it goes into the totals). Tap a photo to see it larger.</li>
    <li><strong>Approve</strong> when it is a real club activity, with a suitable photo or a link to the club's own post, and the photo-consent box is ticked.</li>
    <li><strong>Correct</strong> fixes spelling, shortens text, or removes a phone number before you approve. Do not rewrite the club's story.</li>
    <li><strong>Reject</strong> needs a reason. Tap one of the ready-made reasons or write your own. The club gets it by email.</li>
    <li><strong>Recent:</strong> approved activities and coming events. <strong>★ Story of the month</strong> marks the best activity of the month. <strong>Leave out of bulletin</strong> keeps an item out of Sunday's bulletin. <strong>Hide</strong> takes a published activity off the website (write why; the club is not emailed); <strong>Put back</strong> returns it.</li>
    <li><strong>Roles:</strong> you can also correct a club's President, Secretary or Executive Secretary (see Roles below).</li>
    <li><strong>Saturday 6 pm:</strong> an email shows tomorrow's bulletin. Nothing to do if it looks right. Tap <strong>Leave this out</strong> next to anything that should not go out.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If someone else got there first, the desk says so ("Already approved by …").</p>

  <h2 id="members">Members moderators</h2>
  <p>You check members' consent requests (directory, photo, birthday and anniversary greetings), removal requests and club changes, sent through the My details and Club updates forms by anyone other than the member from their own email. These are never approved from an email, only on the signed-in desk.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consent requests:</strong> check that the photo shows the member alone and is suitable, and read the warnings (declaration not ticked, spouse's agreement missing). Then <strong>Approve</strong> or <strong>Reject</strong> with a reason.</li>
    <li><strong>Removal requests:</strong> tap <strong>Remove now</strong>, within two days. The website drops the details at its next update.</li>
    <li><strong>Club changes:</strong> a member who joined, left, moved to another club or passed away, or a club or district role, sent by anyone through the Club updates form (members and roles). Each one shows what was sent and, below it, what the members list holds for that member ID now. Check they agree (the right person, the right club), then <strong>Approve</strong>: the members list, the club history or the role list is updated and the website follows at its next update. Or <strong>Reject</strong> with a reason, which goes to the sender. <strong>Passed away:</strong> first confirm it with the club, tick <strong>I have confirmed this with the club</strong>, then approve.</li>
    <li><strong>Find a member:</strong> search by name, RI member ID, email or mobile. <strong>Edit</strong> corrects the name, RI member ID, club, status, mobile or email, with a reason. Status also puts right a mistake: set someone marked "left" or "deceased" back to active. A club change is recorded in the member's club history.</li>
    <li><strong>Mark as deceased:</strong> after a search, check it is the right person and club, then confirm. Greetings stop at once.</li>
    <li><strong>Recent changes:</strong> the latest corrections, who made them and why. <strong>Undo</strong> puts the old values back, as long as nobody has changed them again since.</li>
    <li><strong>Roles:</strong> see below.</li>
    <li><strong>Couples waiting:</strong> anniversaries waiting for the other spouse's form. Ask the club to follow up.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="roles">Roles (Content and Members moderators)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Roles to check</strong> (Members moderators): what the daily check found, such as a role with no member ID, the same person under two IDs, or someone holding a role who is marked left. Tap <strong>Open</strong> to find that role.</li>
    <li><strong>Find a role</strong> by name, club or RI member ID. <strong>Change</strong> corrects who holds it (the RI member ID; the name follows the members list) and, for an Assistant Governor, their clubs and area. <strong>End role</strong> is for someone who resigned or was replaced: the website stops showing them, and the record stays.</li>
    <li><strong>Add an office bearer:</strong> a club's President, Secretary or Executive Secretary for this year or next. A club has one of each at a time: end the old role first.</li>
    <li>Content moderators handle club office bearers only; district roles are for Members moderators.</li>
    <li><strong>Who acts now:</strong> until a club tells the district this year's President, Secretary or Executive Secretary, the last known one carries on. The top of the Roles tab counts the clubs still on last year's; in Find a role, each club office bearer shows <em>acts now</em> or <em>acts until this year's is told</em>.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 id="held">Not accepted</h2>
  <p>When the district turns on "only office bearers may send", a club's activity or update sent by someone else does not reach To check: the sender is told by email who can send, and it waits on the <strong>Not accepted</strong> tab. <strong>Let through</strong> sends it to the moderators as usual. If the sender is the club's new office bearer, add them on the Roles tab too (and their email on the members list), so their next form goes straight through.</p>

  <h2 id="admin">Administrators</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Admin → Clubs:</strong> <strong>Add a club</strong> with its RI club ID, name, city, area and charter date; the forms list it at once, and a new club is not counted as quiet for its first 60 days. <strong>Edit</strong> renames a club (the old name is kept, the web address stays) or corrects its city, area or charter date. <strong>Close</strong> moves its members to the club it merged into, or marks them as left.</li>
    <li><strong>Admin → Moderators:</strong> add a moderator (type, name, Google email, areas for Content moderators), change one, or set them inactive. They sign in to the desk with their email; no Sheet access is needed. Nobody can take themselves off the list.</li>
    <li>Each July, when the district team changes, check the moderators list here: the new area moderators in, those who stepped down set to inactive.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="clubs">Club engagement moderators</h2>
  <p>You encourage clubs that have not posted for a while.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Quiet clubs</strong> lists active clubs with no activity in the last 30 days, with the last activity date and who reminded them last.</li>
    <li><strong>Email President and Secretary</strong> sends a friendly reminder with the club's own form link, from the district account and signed "Rotary District 3110 website team". A hidden copy comes to you. Once a week at most per club.</li>
    <li><strong>WhatsApp</strong> opens WhatsApp with a ready message and the club's form link. You choose the person to send it to.</li>
    <li>On the 1st of each month an email lists the same quiet clubs (no activity in the last 30 days).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="office">District office moderators</h2>
  <p>You answer messages from the website's contact form.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Each message comes to you by email. <strong>Do not press Reply on that email</strong>: your own name and email would show.</li>
    <li>On the desk, open <strong>Messages</strong>, tap <strong>Reply</strong> on the message, type your answer and tap <strong>Send</strong>. It goes from the district account, signed "Rotary District 3110", and the message is marked answered. Your answer is kept with the message.</li>
    <li>Someone who gave only a mobile number: call or WhatsApp them from the <strong>district office phone</strong>, not your personal phone. Then tap <strong>Mark answered</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Sunday 8 am:</strong> an email brings the week's bulletin message. Forward it to the district WhatsApp groups.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="practice">The practice round</h2>
  <p>Before the website opens, the administrator starts a practice round. You get an email listing what to try, and practice items made for you appear on the desk, with titles starting "Practice:". They look real, but they are never published, and nobody outside the moderators is emailed.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Content:</strong> approve the tree plantation (try the Approve button in its email); remove the mobile number from the blood donation camp with Correct, then approve; change the dinner's fee to "₹300 per person" with Correct, then approve; reject the old-age home visit (no photo or link) with a reason.</li>
    <li><strong>Members:</strong> reject the consent request of "Practice: Rtn Asha Sharma" (declaration not ticked) with a reason. Then search in Mark as deceased, and do not confirm.</li>
    <li><strong>District office:</strong> reply to "Practice: Ramesh Gupta"; the answer comes to your own inbox, exactly as the public would get it. "Practice: Sunita" gave only a mobile number: do not call it (it is not real), just tap Mark answered.</li>
    <li><strong>Club engagement:</strong> in Quiet clubs, tap WhatsApp for any club and send the message to yourself. Do not tap Email: it really emails the club.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>When you have finished, tell the website administrator.</p>

  <h2 id="help">Something not working?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No code arrives:</strong> look in Spam, check the spelling, and use the email the district has for you. Still nothing: ask the administrator to check the moderators list.</li>
    <li><strong>A link has expired:</strong> email buttons work for 7 days. Open the desk instead; the item is under To check.</li>
    <li><strong>Anything else:</strong> tell the website administrator what you tapped and what the desk said.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><a class="btn btn-gold" href="/desk/">Open the moderation desk</a></p>
</div>
